==German==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schicken||to outfit oneself, fit in, arrange appropriately|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|skigjanan|lang=gem-pro}}, causative of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|geschehen|geschehen, geschēn|to happen, rush|lang=gmh}} from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|giskehan||to happen|lang=goh}} from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|skehanan||to run, move quickly|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|skek-||to run, jump, spring|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|sceon|scēon|to happen|lang=ang}}, ''schie-'' in {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|schielijk||hasty|lang=nl}}. More at {{term|chic|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɪkŋ̩/|/ˈʃɪkən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-schicken.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|De-at-schicken.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
* {{rhymes|ɪkŋ̩|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|schickt|schickte|geschickt}}

# {{transitive|lang=de}} to [[send]]
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to [[hurry]] (rare)
# {{reflexive|lang=de}} to be decent, to be appropriate

